{"name":"Tee Off","hex":"#68855a","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tee off","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hit the first shot of the hole, from the tee.","To hit the ball very hard, especially for a home run."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tee_off"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tee Off","blocks":[{"text":"Tee Off, known in Japan as Golf Shiyō Yo , is a video game developed and published by Bottom Up and Acclaim Entertainment in 1999-2000."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c0/Tee_Off_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tee_Off","wikidata":"Q11303716"},{"title":"Tee","blocks":[{"text":"A tee is a stand used in sport to support and elevate a stationary ball prior to striking with a foot, club, or bat. Tees are used extensively in golf, tee-ball, American football, and rugby. In addition, they are used as training devices for baseball and softball but are not used during gameplay."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/09/Golf_Club_at_Wescott_Plantation_%289321187216%29.jpg/330px-Golf_Club_at_Wescott_Plantation_%289321187216%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tee","wikidata":"Q1938377"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Golf_tees_selection.jpg/500px-Golf_tees_selection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Golf_tees_selection.jpg/1280px-Golf_tees_selection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Golf_tees_selection.jpg/500px-Golf_tees_selection.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Golf tees","link":"https://en.wikipedia.o